==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|la|bipartītus|t=bisected}}, perfect passive participle of {{m|la|bipartiō|t=I divide into two parts, bisect}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/baɪˈpɑːtaɪt/}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Having two [[part]]s.
# {{lb|en|of an agreement or contract}} Having two [[participant]]s; [[joint]].
# {{lb|en|botany|of leaves}} [[divided|Divided]] into two at the [[base]].
# {{lb|en|graph theory|of a graph}} Having [[vertex|vertices]] that can be divided into two [[independent]] [[set]]s (see [[bigraph]])

